    {
      "type": "updated",
      "source": "wgmods",
      "sourceId": "7661",
      "title": "SpotMeter",
      "previous": {
        "modVersion": "7.1.0",
        "wotGameVersion": "2.3.1.1",
        "fileName": "spotmeter-v7.1.0_8glRvc7.wotmod",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-06T21:44:57.316Z",
        "changeLog": "NEW\n- Hover tooltips in the settings menu: every option in the in-garage configurator (a mods-settings menu such as aslainMenu / ModsSettingsAPI) now shows a short hint on hover, in English and Polish - what the option assumes, the exact view-range % for the enemy-loadout toggles and optics/vents/CVS levels, and a note that XVM controls the minimap circle's colour while its minimap is active.\nCHANGED\n- Rebuilt for WoT 2.3.1.1 (minor patch; no other gameplay changes).\nReminder (unchanged since v7.0.0): the in-battle panel is a Gameface overlay and REQUIRES net.openwg.gameface (free, MIT; already in common modpacks). The minimap circle and the hotkeys work even without it."
      },
      "current": {
        "modVersion": "7.2.0",
        "wotGameVersion": "2.3.1.2",
        "fileName": "spotmeter-v7.2.0.wotmod",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T15:18:01.405Z",
        "changeLog": "NEW\n- Circle-colour pickers in the settings menu: the four state colours (moving / still / after firing / camo net) are now editable from the in-garage configurator (a mods-settings menu such as aslainMenu / ModsSettingsAPI) with real colour pickers, instead of hand-editing decimal RGB values in spotmeter.json. The section tooltip reminds you that XVM's minimap, while active, repaints the circle in its own colour and overrides these.\nCHANGED\n- Rebuilt for WoT 2.3.1.2 (minor patch; no other gameplay changes).\nReminder (since v7.0.0): the in-battle panel is a Gameface overlay and REQUIRES net.openwg.gameface (free, MIT; already in common modpacks). The minimap circle and the hotkeys work even without it."
      }
    },
